WHAT TO DO:
Create a new digest package with all Java record DTOs needed for the daily digest email.

STEPS:
3.1 Create package directory: lfiq-backend/src/main/java/com/loanfactory/lfiq/digest/

3.2 Create the following Java records in digest/model/:

    DailyDigestPayload.java:
      public record DailyDigestPayload(
          UUID loId,
          String loFirstName,
          String loEmail,
          LocalDate digestDate,             // the date the digest covers (yesterday in PT)
          List<HotHomeowner> hot,           // size 0-3
          List<RisingHomeowner> rising,     // size 0-N (cap 5 in template render)
          List<NewViewerHomeowner> newViewers, // size 0-N (cap 5)
          YourDayCounters stats,
          String unsubscribeUrl             // pre-built URL with signed token
      ) {
          public boolean isEmpty() {
              return hot.isEmpty()
                  && rising.isEmpty()
                  && newViewers.isEmpty()
                  && stats.isAllZero();
          }
      }

    HotHomeowner.java:
      public record HotHomeowner(
          UUID homeownerId, String fullName, String email,
          String engagementLevel,    // "HIGH"
          int viewedSectionCount,    // count of distinct sections in 24h
          int totalEventCount,
          String topSection,         // e.g., "Refinance"
          String reportUrl
      ) {}

    RisingHomeowner.java:
      public record RisingHomeowner(
          UUID homeownerId, String fullName,
          String previousLevel,      // e.g., "MEDIUM"
          String currentLevel,       // e.g., "HIGH"
          String reportUrl
      ) {}

    NewViewerHomeowner.java:
      public record NewViewerHomeowner(
          UUID homeownerId, String fullName,
          Instant firstViewAt,
          String reportUrl
      ) {}

    YourDayCounters.java:
      public record YourDayCounters(
          int reportsCreated,
          int reportsViewedUniqueHomeowners,
          int totalEngagementEvents
      ) {
          public boolean isAllZero() {
              return reportsCreated == 0
                  && reportsViewedUniqueHomeowners == 0
                  && totalEngagementEvents == 0;
          }
      }

3.3 Unit tests:
    - DailyDigestPayload.isEmpty() returns true when all lists empty and stats.isAllZero() true.
    - DailyDigestPayload.isEmpty() returns false when hot list is non-empty.
    - YourDayCounters.isAllZero() returns true when all counters are 0.
    - YourDayCounters.isAllZero() returns false when any counter > 0.
    Run: ./gradlew test --tests *DailyDigest*

3.4 Acceptance:
    - ./gradlew compileJava clean.
    - ./gradlew test --tests *DailyDigest* passes.

DEPENDENCIES: none (pure DTOs, no DB or service dependencies).

