REPO: lfiq-backend | BRANCH: agent/<bead-id>-saved-filter-scoped-list from feature/saved-filters

DEPENDS ON: task 1.3 (SavedFilterServiceImpl must exist)

FILE TO MODIFY:
  src/main/java/com/loanfactory/lfiq/savedfilter/service/impl/SavedFilterServiceImpl.java

CONTEXT: The list endpoint accepts @SearchEntity DSL ?filter= params AND an optional ?target= convenience param. A hostile client might craft ?filter=user_id eq "<otherUser>" to read another user's data. The user_id predicate MUST always be AND-ed in the service so it cannot be overridden by the incoming filter spec.

IMPLEMENTATION of listByCurrentUser(String target, Pageable pageable, Specification<SavedFilterEntity> searchSpec):

  String currentUserId = SecurityUtils.getCurrentUserId(true);

  Specification<SavedFilterEntity> spec = (root, query, cb) ->
      cb.equal(root.get(SavedFilterEntity.Fields.USER_ID), currentUserId);

  if (target != null && !target.isBlank()) {
      Specification<SavedFilterEntity> targetSpec = (root, query, cb) ->
          cb.equal(root.get(SavedFilterEntity.Fields.TARGET), target);
      spec = spec.and(targetSpec);
  }

  if (searchSpec != null) {
      spec = spec.and(searchSpec);
  }

  // Apply default ordering if pageable has no sort
  if (pageable.getSort().isUnsorted()) {
      pageable = PageRequest.of(pageable.getPageNumber(), pageable.getPageSize(),
          Sort.by(Sort.Order.desc(SavedFilterEntity.Fields.IS_DEFAULT),
                  Sort.Order.asc(SavedFilterEntity.Fields.NAME)));
  }

  return entityService.getAllBy(SavedFilterEntity.class, spec, pageable);

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:
- Even if searchSpec contains user_id condition for another user, results are always scoped to currentUserId
- Default sort is is_default desc, name asc when no sort in pageable
- ./gradlew compileJava passes

