## Implementation Details
Follow the pattern from FeedbackController (src/main/java/com/loanfactory/lfiq/feedback/controller/FeedbackController.java).

```java
package com.loanfactory.lfiq.onboarding.controller;

import com.loanfactory.lfiq.onboarding.entity.OnboardingWorkflowEntity;
import com.loanfactory.lfiq.onboarding.facade.OnboardingWorkflowFacade;
import com.loanfactory.lfiq.onboarding.model.request.UpdateOnboardingStateRequest;
import jakarta.validation.Valid;
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/v1/onboarding-workflow")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class OnboardingWorkflowController {

    private final OnboardingWorkflowFacade onboardingWorkflowFacade;

    @GetMapping("/me")
    public OnboardingWorkflowEntity getMyOnboarding() {
        return onboardingWorkflowFacade.getOrCreateForCurrentUser();
    }

    @PatchMapping("/me")
    public OnboardingWorkflowEntity updateMyOnboarding(
            @Valid @RequestBody final UpdateOnboardingStateRequest request) {
        return onboardingWorkflowFacade.updateForCurrentUser(request);
    }
}
```

Key conventions:
- Base path /v1/onboarding-workflow (matches existing /v1/users, /v1/feedbacks, /v1/reports)
- Controller returns raw entity — tera-core BaseResponseHandler auto-wraps in Response<T> envelope
- @Valid on request body for potential future validation annotations
- Controller is thin: ZERO business logic, only delegates to facade
- @RequiredArgsConstructor for constructor injection
- No @ResponseStatus needed — defaults to 200 OK for both GET and PATCH

## Acceptance Criteria
